# Orders API <%= edit_link %>

> <i class="fa fa-exclamation-triangle"></i>
> **Breaking change for enrolled shops:** Starting from 30/03/2026, for shops enrolled in the mandatory "Set as Ready" program,
> downloading the voucher will no longer automatically mark the order as ready.
> You must explicitly call the `set_as_ready` endpoint. [Read more](#mark-order-as-ready-for-dispatch-set-as-ready)

Orders API allows Skroutz Merchants to perform actions on their Smart Cart orders,
such as accepting or rejecting an order.

You may find a high level overview of the service and descriptive guides for its activation in the
[merchant support guidelines](https://<%= settings.merchants_domain %>/merchants/support/guidelines/skroutz_marketplace_integration).

<%= partial 'partials/toc' %>

## Setup

### Obtaining an API token

In order to be able to use the API, you need to generate an **API token** from within Smart Cart settings
page in merchant's panel (Merchants > Services > [Skroutz Marketplace](https://<%= settings.merchants_domain %>/merchants/account/shop/ecommerce_details)).

> <i class="fa fa-exclamation-triangle"></i>
> There can only be one active **API key** per shop at a certain time.
> Creating a new API key will expire any previous one.

### Authorization

Pass in a valid **API token** in the `Authorization` header, prefixed with `Bearer `
as in the following curl example.

A specific `Accept` header is also required.

<pre class="terminal">
curl -X GET https://<%= settings.api_domain %>/merchants/ecommerce/orders/191128-1234567 \
  -H 'Accept: application/vnd.<%= settings.site_name %>+json; version=3.0' \
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer your_access_token_here'
</pre>

## Endpoints

All endpoints require the order `code` as a URL parameter. This is available in all incoming order
[Webhook](/smart_cart/orders_webhook) events, as well as the merchants' panel.

### Retrieve a single order

When an order is in a state that can be accepted or rejected, `accept_options` and `reject_options`
attributes are included in the response, providing all the available options for
issuing "accept" or "reject" requests for the order, respectively.

Pass `action_options=1` as a query parameter to additionally include `reschedule_options` and
`relocate_options` in the response. These list the currently available pickup dates the order can be
[rescheduled](#reschedule-a-single-orders-pickup) to, and the pickup locations it can be
[relocated](#relocate-a-single-orders-pickup) to. They are omitted by default because they are
time-sensitive: available reschedule dates shrink as time passes and an order can become ineligible,
so you should always fetch the order (with `action_options=1`) right before issuing a reschedule or
relocate request, and use a value from that fresh response.

<pre class="terminal">
  GET /merchants/ecommerce/orders/:code
  GET /merchants/ecommerce/orders/:code?action_options=1
  GET /merchants/ecommerce/orders/:code?compensation_requests=1
</pre>

<%= render_recording :merchants_ecommerce_orders_show %>

#### Example: including reschedule/relocate options

<%= render_recording :merchants_ecommerce_orders_show_action_options %>

With `action_options=1`, an accepted order additionally carries the two option lists
(`reschedule_options` and `relocate_options`; only the relevant attributes are shown above).
Both lists are empty (`[]`) when the order cannot be rescheduled/relocated, and both are omitted
entirely when `action_options=1` is not passed.

#### Compensation requests on the order

Pass `compensation_requests=1` as a query parameter to include the order's
[compensation requests](#file-a-compensation-request) in `compensation_requests`, oldest first, under
the id each request was filed with. Each carries its state and, for each line item, the amount once
approved or the reason once rejected, as the merchants' panel shows them. The list is empty (`[]`) when
the order has none. Without the parameter, and in order webhooks, the attribute is omitted.

<pre class="terminal">
  GET /merchants/ecommerce/orders/:code?compensation_requests=1
</pre>

<%= render_code '{
  "order": {
    "code": "191128-1234567",
    "state": "returned",
    "compensation_requests": [
      {
        "id": "xK3mPq7Lw2",
        "state": "partially_approved",
        "created_at": "2026-11-04T16:35:37+02:00",
        "line_items": [
          {
            "id": "k9Qp2xR4mN",
            "quantity": 2,
            "reason": "damaged_packaging",
            "state": "approved",
            "compensation_amount": 25.0
          },
          {
            "id": "7mWq1zT8bV",
            "quantity": 1,
            "reason": "damaged_product",
            "state": "rejected",
            "rejection_reason": "The photos show no damage"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}', 'javascript' %>

Only the relevant attributes are shown above. No webhook is sent when a request is decided: to learn
the decision, retrieve the order with `compensation_requests=1`.

### Accept a single order

To accept an order you need to provide the `pickup_location` and the `pickup_window` which are required. You can also specify `number_of_parcels` which is optional with a default value of `1` if missing.

> <i class="fa fa-exclamation-triangle"></i>
> Express orders cannot be accepted via the API. An automated mechanism will handle the order acceptance.

The available param values used are provided in `accept_options` when retrieving a single order.

Each entry of `accept_options.pickup_location` lists the pickup windows available for that
location under `pickup_window`. Send the `pickup_location` together with the `id` of one of its own
windows (e.g. `"20191204T1000-20191204T1200"`), since the available windows may differ per location.
A window ID that isn't available for the given location is rejected with an `Invalid pickup window` error.

Integer `pickup_window` IDs from the top-level `accept_options.pickup_window` list are still
accepted.

<pre class="terminal">
  POST /merchants/ecommerce/orders/:code/accept
</pre>

<%= render_recording :merchants_ecommerce_orders_accept %>

#### Example
<pre class="terminal">
curl -X POST https://<%= settings.api_domain %>/merchants/ecommerce/orders/191128-1234567/accept \
  -H 'Accept: application/vnd.<%= settings.site_name %>+json; version=3.0' \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8' \
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer your_access_token_here' \
  -d '{ "pickup_location": "YlpD0KROym", "pickup_window": "20191204T1000-20191204T1200", "number_of_parcels": 1 }'
</pre>

### Reschedule a single order's pickup

Changes the pickup **date** of an accepted order.

Retrieve the order with [`?action_options=1`](#retrieve-a-single-order) and read `reschedule_options`.
Send one of the returned `date` values (an `YYYY-MM-DD` string) as the `reschedule_date` param.

> <i class="fa fa-exclamation-triangle"></i>
> Available dates are time-sensitive. Always fetch the order right before rescheduling and send a
> `date` from that fresh `reschedule_options` list. A date that is no longer available is rejected
> (rather than silently applied to a different date).

<pre class="terminal">
  POST /merchants/ecommerce/orders/:code/reschedule_pickup
</pre>

<%= render_recording :merchants_ecommerce_orders_reschedule_pickup %>

#### Example
<pre class="terminal">
curl -X POST https://<%= settings.api_domain %>/merchants/ecommerce/orders/191128-1234567/reschedule_pickup \
  -H 'Accept: application/vnd.<%= settings.site_name %>+json; version=3.0' \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8' \
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer your_access_token_here' \
  -d '{ "reschedule_date": "2026-09-25" }'
</pre>

#### Error Responses

**Invalid or no longer available date** (missing, malformed, or not in `reschedule_options` — re-fetch and retry):

<pre class="terminal">
HTTP/1.1 422 Unprocessable Entity
</pre>

<%= render_code '{
  "errors": [
    {
      "code": "reschedule_date",
      "messages": [
        "Invalid reschedule date"
      ]
    }
  ]
}', 'javascript' %>

**Order not eligible for rescheduling** (e.g. fulfilled by Skroutz, fulfilled by merchant, store pickup, express). The `messages` describe the specific reason:

<pre class="terminal">
HTTP/1.1 422 Unprocessable Entity
</pre>

<%= render_code '{
  "errors": [
    {
      "code": "order_status",
      "messages": [
        "Order rescheduling is not supported for \"Fulfilled by Skroutz\" orders."
      ]
    }
  ]
}', 'javascript' %>

### Relocate a single order's pickup

Changes the pickup **location** of an accepted order, keeping the current pickup date/slot. The
courier is re-selected for the new location automatically, and a new voucher may be issued.

Retrieve the order with [`?action_options=1`](#retrieve-a-single-order) and read `relocate_options`.
Send one of the returned location `id` values as the `pickup_location` param. The order's current
location is excluded from the list.

> <i class="fa fa-exclamation-triangle"></i>
> Available only for orders that have more than one pickup location configured for the shop and are
> not fulfilled by Skroutz/merchant, store pickup or express.

<pre class="terminal">
  POST /merchants/ecommerce/orders/:code/relocate_pickup
</pre>

<%= render_recording :merchants_ecommerce_orders_relocate_pickup %>

#### Example
<pre class="terminal">
curl -X POST https://<%= settings.api_domain %>/merchants/ecommerce/orders/191128-1234567/relocate_pickup \
  -H 'Accept: application/vnd.<%= settings.site_name %>+json; version=3.0' \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8' \
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer your_access_token_here' \
  -d '{ "pickup_location": "m8O6n3eO6j" }'
</pre>

#### Error Responses

**Invalid pickup location** (missing, not one of the shop's locations, or the order's current location):

<pre class="terminal">
HTTP/1.1 422 Unprocessable Entity
</pre>

<%= render_code '{
  "errors": [
    {
      "code": "pickup_location",
      "messages": [
        "Invalid pickup location"
      ]
    }
  ]
}', 'javascript' %>

**Order not eligible for relocation** (e.g. single pickup location, fulfilled by Skroutz/merchant, express). The `messages` describe the specific reason:

<pre class="terminal">
HTTP/1.1 422 Unprocessable Entity
</pre>

<%= render_code '{
  "errors": [
    {
      "code": "order_status",
      "messages": [
        "Pickup relocation is not supported for this order."
      ]
    }
  ]
}', 'javascript' %>

### Reject a single order

#### Reject specific line items with reasons

To reject specific line items you need to provide a `line_items` params which would hold an
array of line items. Each line items should have the line item `id` and the rejection
`reason_id`. In case the rejection reason `requires_available_quantity`,
an `available_quantity` attribute is also required.

The available rejection reason IDs are provided in `reject_options` when retrieving a single order.

<pre class="terminal">
  POST /merchants/ecommerce/orders/:code/reject
</pre>

<%= render_recording :merchants_ecommerce_orders_reject %>

#### Example
<pre class="terminal">
curl -X POST https://<%= settings.api_domain %>/merchants/ecommerce/orders/191128-1234567/reject \
  -H 'Accept: application/vnd.<%= settings.site_name %>+json; version=3.0' \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8' \
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer your_access_token_here' \
  -d '{ "line_items": [ { "id": "jn231kb12u", "reason_id": 2 }, { "id": "opaoe8M3pZ", "reason_id": 4, "available_quantity": 1 } ] }'
</pre>

#### Reject whole order with "other" reason

<pre class="terminal">
  POST /merchants/ecommerce/orders/:code/reject
</pre>

<%= render_recording :merchants_ecommerce_orders_reject_other %>

#### Example
<pre class="terminal">
curl -X POST https://<%= settings.api_domain %>/merchants/ecommerce/orders/191128-1234567/reject \
  -H 'Accept: application/vnd.<%= settings.site_name %>+json; version=3.0' \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8' \
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer your_access_token_here' \
  -d '{ "rejection_reason_other": "Our store is closed for personal reasons" }'
</pre>

### Upload receipt/invoice

To upload the receipt/invoice of the order, you need to set the `invoice_file` param with the contents of the document.

<pre class="terminal">
  POST /merchants/ecommerce/orders/:code/invoices
</pre>

#### Example
<pre class="terminal">
curl -X POST https://<%= settings.api_domain %>/merchants/ecommerce/orders/191128-1234567/invoices \
  -H 'Accept: application/vnd.<%= settings.site_name %>+json; version=3.0' \
  -H 'Content-Type: multipart/form-data' \
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer your_access_token_here' \
  -F 'invoice_file=@/path/to/invoice.pdf'
</pre>

<%= partial 'localizable/smart_cart/invoice_upload_notes' %>

### Upload credit invoice

To upload the credit invoice of the order, you need to set the `credit_invoice_file` param with the contents of the document.

A credit invoice is expected for orders that were cancelled, returned, partially returned or returned to sender
after a fiscal document had already been issued for them.

<pre class="terminal">
  POST /merchants/ecommerce/orders/:code/credit_invoices
</pre>

#### Example
<pre class="terminal">
curl -X POST https://<%= settings.api_domain %>/merchants/ecommerce/orders/191128-1234567/credit_invoices \
  -H 'Accept: application/vnd.<%= settings.site_name %>+json; version=3.0' \
  -H 'Content-Type: multipart/form-data' \
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer your_access_token_here' \
  -F 'credit_invoice_file=@/path/to/credit_invoice.pdf'
</pre>

<%= partial 'localizable/smart_cart/invoice_upload_notes' %>

#### Success Response

<pre class="terminal">
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Type: application/json
</pre>

<%= render_code '{
  "success": true
}', 'javascript' %>

#### Error Responses

**No file submitted** (the `credit_invoice_file` param is missing, or was not sent as a `multipart/form-data` file):

<pre class="terminal">
HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request
</pre>

<%= render_code '{
  "errors": [
    {
      "code": "credit_invoice_file",
      "messages": [
        "Missing credit invoice file"
      ]
    }
  ]
}', 'javascript' %>

**Order has not been accepted yet:**

<pre class="terminal">
HTTP/1.1 422 Unprocessable Entity
</pre>

<%= render_code '{
  "errors": [
    {
      "code": "credit_invoice_file",
