### Mark order as ready for dispatch (Set as Ready)

For shops with `set_as_ready_required: true` in the [order response](#retrieve-a-single-order),
the courier Skroutz Last Mile (SLM) will only pick up orders that have been explicitly marked as ready for dispatch.
This applies only to orders shipped via Skroutz Last Mile.

| Before | After (for enrolled shops) |
| ------ | -------------------------- |
| Downloading the voucher via API automatically marks the order as ready for dispatch | Downloading the voucher only downloads the voucher |
| No explicit "ready" signal needed | You must call `POST /merchants/ecommerce/orders/:code/set_as_ready` to mark the order as ready |
| N/A | You can call `POST /merchants/ecommerce/orders/:code/set_as_not_ready` to undo (if order hasn't been picked up) |

**Shops not enrolled** (default behavior): No changes. Voucher download continues to auto-mark as ready.

Marking an order as ready:

* Marks the order as ready for pickup by the courier
* Triggers auto-reschedule to an earlier pickup window (if available)
* Notifies the courier (SLM) that the order is ready for shipping

**Prerequisites:**

* Order must be in `accepted` state
* Order must not already be marked as ready
* Order must be shipped via Skroutz Last Mile (SLM)
* Order must be a core marketplace order (not FBM, not FBS, not store pickup)

<pre class="terminal">
  POST /merchants/ecommerce/orders/:code/set_as_ready
</pre>

No request body required.

#### Example
<pre class="terminal">
curl -X POST https://<%= settings.api_domain %>/merchants/ecommerce/orders/260225-123456/set_as_ready \
  -H 'Accept: application/vnd.<%= settings.site_name %>+json; version=3.0' \
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer your_access_token_here'
</pre>

#### Success Response

<pre class="terminal">
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Type: application/json
</pre>

<%= render_code '{
  "success": true
}', 'javascript' %>

#### Error Responses

**Order not found:**

<pre class="terminal">
HTTP/1.1 404 Not Found
</pre>

<%= render_code '{
  "errors": [
    {
      "code": "order_error",
      "messages": [
        "Order not found"
      ]
    }
  ]
}', 'javascript' %>

**Order not eligible** (wrong state, already ready, etc.):

<pre class="terminal">
HTTP/1.1 422 Unprocessable Entity
</pre>

<%= render_code '{
  "errors": [
    {
      "code": "order_error",
      "messages": [
        "Order is not eligible to be marked as ready"
      ]
    }
  ]
}', 'javascript' %>

